            <OtherClusion>
                <InclusionCriterion>- Patients aged 18 or older, male or female, who were either hospitalized or receiving outpatient care at the time of enrollment.

- Diagnosis of a current alcohol use disorder, according to the diagnostic criteria in the DSM-5-TR.

- Native French speaker, able to read and write fluently in French (based on personality questionnaires and cognitive tests).

- Voluntary participation, following review of the information sheet describing the study and written agreement to participate by signing the informed consent form.</InclusionCriterion>
                <ExclusionCriterion>Exclusion criteria:

- Diagnosis of active and unstable psychiatric disorders, based on the DSM-5-RT diagnostic criteria.

- Presence of moderate or severe substance use disorders according to DSM-5-TR criteria (excluding tobacco).

- A diagnosis of intellectual disability or pervasive developmental disorder.

- Presence of any clinically significant or unstable condition: organic disorders affecting the central nervous system or conditions likely to interfere with assessments, including neurological complications of alcoholism.

- Presence of uncorrected sensory impairments (vision and hearing) due to the perceptual-visual nature of certain cognitive tests.

- Persons who are specifically protected under Articles L.1121-5 through L.1121-8 of the French Public Health Code.



Exclusion criteria:

- Patients with cognitive impairment (Montreal Cognitive Assessment [MoCA] score &lt; 22 at baseline).</ExclusionCriterion>
            </OtherClusion>
